# Test: informational note on a converted rate × duration, and a clear
# "not a rate" error for `over` on an amount.
# Given: rate = $20/hour, dpw = 3 days, weekly = 8 * rate * dpw,
#        total_amount = weekly over 1 year
# Expected: weekly keeps its value ($11,520.00 — 8 × $20/h × 72 h) and
#           carries the note "3 days = 72 hours (rate is per hour) ..."
#           total_amount errors: weekly is an amount, not a rate.
run observe=results
----
-- results:
Line 0 (# Wages): value=, error=""
Line 1 (rate = $20/hour): value=$20.00/h, error=""
Line 2 (dpw = 3 days): value=3 day, error=""
Line 3 (weekly = 8 * rate * dpw): value=$11,520.00, error="", note="3 days = 72 hours (rate is per hour). For a working day, write the hours explicitly, e.g. 8 hours/day"
